c/modules/logs/\n```\n\nSo `PROJECT_ROOT` resolves to **`src/modules/`**, which means `setup_logging()` writes to **`src/modules/logs/`** — that\'s exactly the untracked directory we\'re seeing in `git status`.\n\n## All other files just use `logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)` — none of them set up their own handlers or write to a different path. The `setup_logging()` call in `app.py` is the single point where logging is initialized.\n\nSo the issue is clear: **`PROJECT_ROOT` is one (or two) levels too deep.** It currently resolves to `src/modules/` instead of the actual project root. The log files are landing in `src/modules/logs/` when they should be landing in the project root\'s `logs/`.\n\nWant me to fix the path? It needs an extra `.parent` (→ `src/`) or two (→ the repo root, where `src/` lives), depending on where you want the `logs/` folder to sit.', created_at='Oct 04, 02:25 PM', speaker_name='Amadeus', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=67, session_id=3, role='user', text='alright fix it', created_at='Oct 04, 02:26 PM', speaker_name='toffeezzz', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=68, session_id=3, role='assistant', text='Let me read the file first, then fix it.\n\n---\n\nActually, let me count the directory tree:\n\n```\nrepo-root/          ← This is where you want logs/\n├── src/\n│   ├── modules/\n│   │   ├── utils/\n│   │   │   └── logger.py   ← __file__\n│   │   └── logs/           ← current (wrong) location\n```\n\nCurrent path: `Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent` → `src/modules/`\nNeeds: 4 levels up → repo root\n\nLet me verify by reading the file and checking the actual resolved path.', created_at='Oct 04, 02:26 PM', speaker_name='Amadeus', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=69, session_id=3, role='user', text='go ahead', created_at='Oct 04, 02:27 PM', speaker_name='toffeezzz', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=70, session_id=3, role='assistant', text='Done. `PROJECT_ROOT` now walks up 4 parents from `logger.py` (`src/modules/utils/logger.py` → repo root),