00000"`, `font.pixelSize: 11`\n- `SessionRow.qml`: `"red"`, `"white"`\n- `CustomRect.qml`: `"magenta"`\n- `LeftPanel.qml`: `font.pixelSize: 20`, `font.pixelSize: 16`\n- `InputField.qml`: `font.pixelSize: 30`, `font.pixelSize: 22`\n- `Attachment.qml`: `font.pixelSize: 8`\n\nSo I need to ensure the theme has the right tokens for each of these:\n\nFor `"red"` — the theme has `accentDefault: "#c0392b"` but the original file says `"red"`. Hmm, but the user said "only colors then font" and I should be careful not to change anything. But `"red"` and `"#c0392b"` are different colors! Let me check if the reverted version uses `"red"` or if it was changed to `"#c0392b"` by the previous commits...\n\nThe reverted version should be back to `"red"` since the user said they reverted everything. So I need to add a `colorRed` token, or just... wait, the user wants colors and font sizes. So I should put the EXACT same color values in the theme. So the theme needs `"red"` as a color value for the session row.\n\nActually, let me think more carefully. The point of centralizing is so you can change colors later. So the name in the theme should be descriptive of the *usage*, not the value. So `SessionRow.qml` uses `"red"` for the selected session — the theme could call it `selectedSessionBg` or whatever. But the VALUE should stay `"red"` (not `"#c0392b"`) because I\'m not supposed to change colors.\n\nBut wait — `Main.qml` already uses `"#c0392b"` as an accent color (the toast border). That\'s the same usage as "red" in SessionRow — both indicate "selected/error/accent". Should I make them the same token? The user might want them independently customizable. Let me keep them separate for now and just match what\'s in the code.\n\nLet me add a `colorRed: "red"` to the theme and use that. And for `"white"` I already have `sessionBg` as `"#ffffff"` which is actually the same as `"white"`... wait, it is. Let me just add more color tokens.\n\nI think the cleanest approach: just add color tokens that exactly match the current hardcoded values. If the user wants to consolidate later, that\'s trivial.\n\nLet me rewrite the theme with all the exact values:\n\nCurrent files use:\n- `"#c0392b"` (Main.qml toast accent)\n- `"#27ae60"` (Main.qml "green" — but wait, `show(message, "green")` passes the string `"green"` not a hex code. So the theme doesn\'t need to cover this since it\'s passed dynamically)\n- Actually, in Main.qml: `accent: "#c0392b"` and `show(message, "green")` passes `color` as `"green"` which gets assigned to `accent`. So the theme doesn\'t need a color for "green" — it\'s passed as a parameter.\n- `"#2a2a2a"` (Main.qml toast background)\n- `"white"` (Main.qml toast text, SessionRow.qml unselected)\n- `"gray"` (ChatPanel.qml thinking dots and thinking label)\n- `"#1e1e1e"` (MessageBubble.qml code block background)\n- `"#888888"` (MessageBubble.qml code lang label)\n- `"#d4d4d4"` (MessageBubble.qml code text)\n- `"#33000000"` (MessageBubble.qml attachment fallback)\n- `"red"` (SessionRow.qml selected session)\n- `"magenta"` (CustomRect.qml debug border)\n\nFont sizes:\n- 30 (ChatPanel welcome/greeting, InputField upload button)\n- 22 (InputField send/stop button)\n- 20 (LeftPanel "Agents" header)\n- 16 (LeftPanel "Sessions" header)\n- 11 (MessageBubble code lang label + attachment name)\n- 8 (Attachment compact label)\n\nMy current theme has `fontSm: 11` and `fontXs: 8`, `fontSection: 20`, `fontSubsection: 16`, `fontXl: 30`, `fontLg: 22`. That matches well. Let me also make sure the color tokens are in sync.\n\nLet me rewrite the theme with the rightNow let me update the theme to include exactly the colors from each file (no value changes), then update each QML file.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "Now let me update each QML file to reference the theme. I'll do the simple ones first."}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Now the remaining files. Let me update them.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Now let me check git status to see ever