**Summary of changes:**

**`generic/CustomRect.qml`** — Set default `color: Theme.surfaceContainer` and a debug outline using `Theme.debugOutline` instead of hardcoded magenta.

**`generic/Theme.qml`** — Untouched. Already had the full MD3 palette plus the aliases I needed (like `textPrimary`, `bgCode`, `selectedSessionBg`, etc.).

**`left_panel/AgentRow.qml`** — Agent name text now uses `Theme.textPrimary`.

**`left_panel/LeftPanel.qml`** — "Agents", "Sessions", and "New Session" labels all use `Theme.textPrimary`.

**`left_panel/SessionRow.qml`** — Session row background is now `Theme.selectedSessionBg` (primary container) when selected, `Theme.sessionBg` (surface container) when not. Session title text and delete dialog text use `Theme.textPrimary`.

**`right_panel/ChatPanel.qml`** — Welcome / prompt text uses `Theme.textPrimary`. Thinking footer dots and "Thinking…" label use `Theme.textMuted`.

**`right_panel/MessageBubble.qml`** — User bubbles get `Theme.primaryContainer` background, assistant bubbles get `Theme.surfaceContainer`. All message body text uses `Theme.textPrimary`. Code blocks: background `Theme.bgCode`, language label `Theme.textMuted`, code text `Theme.textCode`. Attachment fallback uses `Theme.bgAttachmentFallback`.

**`right_panel/Attachment.qml`** — Non-image attachment names use `Theme.textDimmed`. Remove button uses `Theme.textPrimary`.

**`right_panel/InputField.qml`** — Input text: `Theme.textPrimary`, placeholder: `Theme.textMuted`. Upload and send button text: `Theme.textPrimary`.

**`Main.qml`** — Toast popup gets `Theme.bgToast` background, `Theme.textPrimary` text, and uses `Theme.accentDefault` / `Theme.accentGreen` for the accent border color instead of hardcoded `#c0392b` / `"green"`.

Every write is tagged with `[amadeus]` inline so there's provenance on the changes. Should be consistent MD3 surfaces across the board — dark container surfaces for backgrounds, lavender-toned primary containers for user messages, and the right contrast colors for text on each.
