2026-10-04 15:18:08 | DEBUG    | modules.agents.models:130 | Say (full): [User toffeezzz] Im your creator and I need help in building you more


TASK: Apply the MD3 dark-purple theme across the QML GUI, replace the stock
Buttons with a custom styled button, and make the panels visually separated.
This is QML only. Do NOT touch any Python, and do NOT change behaviour,
bindings, ids, signals or the scroll/stickToEnd logic in ChatPanel.qml.

Work in src/modules/gui/components/. Make the changes in the order below and
finish each step before starting the next.

## STEP 0: Make Theme work (do this first, QML errors cascade)

Theme.qml is a `pragma Singleton`. It only resolves if a qmldir registers it.
- Put it in its own folder: components/theme/Theme.qml
- Create components/theme/qmldir with exactly one line:
    singleton Theme 1.0 Theme.qml
- In every file that uses Theme, add:  import "../theme"
  (use the right relative path; from components/ root it is "./theme")
- NEVER write `import "../generic/Theme.qml" as Theme`. QML cannot import a
  single .qml file, and the alias would shadow the singleton. If any file
  has that line, delete it.
- NEVER write `Theme {}`. Always use it as `Theme.primary`.
- Do NOT create a qmldir in components/generic (it would hide every type
  that is not listed).
- Property names starting with "on" + capital letter are parsed as signal
  handlers. That is why MD3 "on" roles are suffixed: primaryOn,
  surfaceOn, primaryContainerOn. Never name a property onSomething.

## STEP 1: Theme tokens

Keep all existing colour tokens in Theme.qml. Add font sizes and shape tokens
so components never hardcode numbers:

  fonts:   fontXl 30, fontLg 22, fontMd 14, fontSm 11
  radius:  radiusSm 8, radiusMd 12, radiusLg 16, radiusXl 28, radiusFull 999
  spacing: spaceXs 4, spaceSm 8, spaceMd 12, spaceLg 16, panelGap 12
  sizes:   buttonHeight 40, iconButton 40
  motion:  animFast 100, animNormal 150

Update the header comment of Theme.qml to say colours, fonts, radius, spacing
and motion live here.

## STEP 2: AppButton (components/generic/AppButton.qml)

Create one reusable button based on QtQuick.Controls Button, with custom
`background` and `contentItem`. Never use the default styled Button anywhere.

API:
  property string variant: "filled"   // "filled" | "tonal" | "outlined" | "text"
  property bool iconOnly: false
  text, enabled, onClicked: as normal Button

Look per variant:
  filled   : bg Theme.primary,                text Theme.primaryOn
  tonal    : bg Theme.secondaryContainer,     text Theme.secondaryContainerOn
  outlined : transparent bg, 1px Theme.outline border, text Theme.primary
  text     : transparent bg,                  text Theme.primary

Shape: radius Theme.radiusFull (pill) for text buttons, perfect circle for
iconOnly (width == height == Theme.iconButton). Height Theme.buttonHeight,
horizontal padding Theme.spaceLg. Font Theme.fontMd.

States: draw them with an overlay Rectangle on top of the background, filled
with the text colour:
  hovered  -> overlay opacity 0.08
  pressed  -> overlay opacity 0.12
  focused (visualFocus) -> 2px Theme.primary outline ring
  disabled -> whole button opacity 0.38, no hover effect
Use Behavior on opacity/color with Theme.animFast. Add a HoverHandler with
cursorShape Qt.PointingHandCursor (only while enabled). No scale or rotation
effects on the button itself.

Also create a "danger" look for destructive actions: bg Theme.errorContainer,
text Theme.errorContainerOn. Expose it as variant: "danger".

## STEP 3: Replace every Button

Search all .qml files for `Button {` and replace each with AppButton:
  - Upload "+" in InputField: variant "text", iconOnly. KEEP its existing
    hover rotation animation.
  - Send/Stop in InputField: variant "filled", iconOnly. Keep the existing
    enabled logic and the text switch (send arrow vs stop square). When
    generating, use variant "danger"... no, keep "filled" but it must stay
    visible; Stop must stay always enabled.
  - Attachment remove "X": variant "tonal", iconOnly, size Theme.buttonSm-ish
    (24x24 is fine, override width/height).
  - New Session, delete session, etc. in the left panel: "tonal" for New
    Session, "danger" for delete, "text" for minor actions.
Keep every onClicked handler exactly as it is.

## STEP 4: Layout and separation rules

Principle: separate panels with SPACE and TONE, never with borders.
  - Window/app root background: Theme.background
  - Add Theme.panelGap (12) margin around the whole app and between panels,
    so the root background shows through as the divider.
  - Left panel and the chat area are "cards":
      color Theme.surfaceContainerLow, radius Theme.radiusLg, no border
  - The input bar is a card on top of the chat card:
      color Theme.surfaceContainerHigh, radius Theme.radiusXl
  - Inner list items (session rows, agent rows) use radius Theme.radiusMd.
  - Nesting rule: a child's radius must be smaller than its parent's, and
    inner padding should equal parent radius / 2 or more so corners look
    concentric.
  - Elevation is expressed by tone, not shadows: lowest -> low -> container
    -> high -> highest as things get closer to the user.
  - Dividers, if truly needed: 1px Theme.outlineVariant, never Theme.outline.
Update CustomRect.qml so it takes its default color/radius from Theme
(color Theme.surfaceContainerLow, radius Theme.radiusLg). Keep its debug
outline feature using Theme.debugOutline.

## STEP 5: Component colours

  Session row: default transparent; hover Theme.surfaceContainerHigh;
               selected Theme.secondaryContainer with Theme.secondaryContainerOn text.
  Agent row:   same as session row, selected state gets a 2px Theme.primary ring
               around the avatar.
  User message bubble:  Theme.primaryContainer, text Theme.primaryContainerOn
  Agent message bubble: Theme.surfaceContainerHigh, text Theme.surfaceOn
  Bubble radius Theme.radiusLg, with the corner nearest the sender reduced to
  Theme.spaceXs (bottom-right for user, bottom-left for agent) if the bubble
  is implemented in a way that allows it; otherwise uniform radius.
  Code blocks: Theme.bgCode background, Theme.textCode text, Theme.radiusMd.
  Input TextArea: transparent background, text Theme.surfaceOn,
                  placeholder Theme.textMuted.
  Thinking dots / label: Theme.textDimmed.
  Toasts: Theme.bgToast background, Theme.textPrimary text,
          Theme.accentDefault for errors and Theme.accentGreen for success.
  Scrollbar handle: Theme.outline at 50% opacity, rounded.
  All text default colour: Theme.surfaceOn (QML Text defaults to black,
  which is unreadable on dark).

## RULES

  - No hardcoded colour, font size, radius or spacing literals left in the
    components (0, 1 and tiny layout math are fine).
  - Do not rename ids, properties or signals that Python or other QML
    files reference.
  - Do not change anything in ChatPanel.qml beyond colours/fonts/radius.
  - Report a list of files changed. Do not add new features.
