 empty bottom bar aren\'t "hard to differentiate" — they were never differentiated to begin with. Debug outlines were you drawing in the missing structure by hand.\n\nA couple of side-notes while I was in there:\n- `CustomRect.debugVisible` defaults to `true`. So every card ships pink in the working tree. That should be `false`, and wired to one global `controller.debug` flag so you flip it once, not per-file.\n- `newSessionBtn` is `scale: 0.9` to fake being smaller — so it never really fills its width. That\'s why it looks like a floating bordered pill instead of a row.\n\n**the fix, per area**\n\n1. **One card, not four.** Keep `LeftPanel` as the single `surfaceContainerLow` card. Delete the background from `agentMenu` and `settingsBar` — make them plain `Item`/`ColumnLayout`s.\n2. **Separate sections with a rule, not a tone.** Since rows already hover to `surfaceContainerHigh`, the section bg has to stay `Low` or hover dies. So boundaries come from 1px `Theme.outlineVariant` dividers: one under the "Agents" header, one above the settings bar. That\'s the clean MD3 move — tonal layering can\'t save you when every layer is one step from the next.\n3. **Give the two lists different shapes so you can tell them apart at a glance** — agents are 70px with avatars, sessions are 35px with a bullet. They already differ; the problem is purely that nothing separates the *regions*. Header styling should match on both ("Agents" / "Sessions" same size, weight, left-aligned instead of the current fontLg-vs-fontMd, centered mismatch).\n4. **Session rows need an idle chip.** Right now idle = fully transparent, so an unselected row has no shape. Give it `surfaceContainer` at rest, `surfaceContainerHigh` on hover, `secondaryContainer` on selected — now the row reads even when it\'s not touched.\n5. **`newSessionBtn`:** drop the `scale: 0.9`, make it `surfaceContainerHigh` (or an outlined chip), left-align the label like the rows. It should look like a row you can press, not a button bolted into the panel.\n6. **That bottom-left bar.** It\'s a 96px empty `CustomRect` — post-fix it\'d be a bare strip. What\'s it *supposed* to be? If it\'s a settings/menu holder I can style it as a proper footer; if it\'s still placeholder I\'d rather shrink it to nothing than ship a mystery band.\n\nI\'m leaning dividers + per-row idle chips, since it keeps your hover states intact and stops the panel from becoming a bullseye of concentric tone steps.\n\nBefore I start editing: the tree\'s got uncommitted changes from amadeus across all the left-panel files, so I don\'t want to stomp anything mid-flight. Want me to go ahead on that direction, and what goes in the bottom bar?', created_at='Oct 04, 05:12 PM', speaker_name='Ame', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=178, session_id=14, role='user', text='you know what, before that actually can you strip all the comments from each one and then commit then. group similar diffs to one commit', created_at='Oct 04, 05:36 PM', speaker_name='toffeezzz', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=179, session_id=14, role='assistant', text="Alright, let me see what we're actually working with first.", created_at='Oct 04, 05:36 PM', speaker_name='Ame', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=180, session_id=14, role='assistant', text="Let me look at what's actually in these diffs before I touch anything.", created_at='Oct 04, 05:37 PM', speaker_name='Ame', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=181, session_id=14, role='assistant', text='Okay, before I start yanking comments out of anything, let me see the rest of the changeset so I know what "similar diffs" even means here.', created_at='Oct 04, 05:39 PM', speaker_name='Ame', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=182, session_id=14, role='assistant', text="Let me see the rest of the changeset and what's untracked.", created_at='Oct 04, 05:39 PM', speaker_name='Ame', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=183, session_id=14, role='assistant', text="Okay, I've now read the whole diff. It's basically one big theme refactor by